thermal: core: export thermal_zone_device_set_policy() to modules

A zone registered from the device tree takes the default governor: thermal_of builds the zone's parameters
itself, so a sensor driver cannot name a governor for the one zone it serves. On the UMS9620 boards the stock
zone soc-thmzone (sensor: the out-of-tree mu300_thermal) is the one zone with passive trips, a sustainable
power and weighted cpufreq cooling maps, which is what power_allocator is made for; the nineteen physical zones
have no trips and no cooling devices, and power_allocator as the default would only log "sustainable_power will
be estimated" for each of them. Exported, the sensor driver picks the governor of its own zone right after
registering it, the same call a write to the zone's sysfs "policy" makes; a governor that refuses to bind leaves
the zone with its previous one.

--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
@@ -153,6 +153,7 @@

 	return ret;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(thermal_zone_device_set_policy);

 int thermal_build_list_of_policies(char *buf)
 {
--- a/include/linux/thermal.h
+++ b/include/linux/thermal.h
@@ -313,6 +313,7 @@
 int thermal_zone_device_enable(struct thermal_zone_device *tz);
 int thermal_zone_device_disable(struct thermal_zone_device *tz);
 void thermal_zone_device_critical(struct thermal_zone_device *tz);
+int thermal_zone_device_set_policy(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, char *policy);

 void thermal_pm_prepare(void);
 void thermal_pm_complete(void);
@@ -387,6 +388,9 @@
 static inline int thermal_zone_device_disable(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
 { return -ENODEV; }

+static inline int thermal_zone_device_set_policy(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, char *policy)
+{ return -ENODEV; }
+
 static inline void thermal_pm_prepare(void) {}
 static inline void thermal_pm_complete(void) {}
 #endif /* CONFIG_THERMAL */
